<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Europe</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Europe</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-eu</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:42:34Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-eu" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1433?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-eu" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Ukrainian President Zelenskyy speaks at EU summit amid spat with Donald Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:77e83cd9bbd88578a113392223db031e408ece08ea7455ca51317b3bc82aa341</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:42:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T19:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukrainian-president-zelenskyy-speaks-at-eu-summit-amid-spat-with-donald-trump/a-79684340--6307cb90b3ba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukrainian-president-zelenskyy-speaks-at-eu-summit-amid-spat-with-donald-trump/a-79684340?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">EU leaders reaffirmed support for Ukraine at the Brussels summit. But souring relations with the US over Russia and Starlink and a big hole in the budget will make for a difficult winter for Ukraine.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Hijab ban at schools in Azerbaijan: What's behind the rare wave of protests?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d22f518e7985b7ad375c0bacc21c4bf9f63e49038f3a6a34403f73440b6419f2</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T17:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hijab-ban-at-schools-in-azerbaijan-what-s-behind-the-rare-wave-of-protests/a-79683716--35e52a17baf3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hijab-ban-at-schools-in-azerbaijan-what-s-behind-the-rare-wave-of-protests/a-79683716?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Girls wearing headscarves have been turned away from schools in Azerbaijan, triggering unusual protests involving children. The government rules do not mention hijabs. Why are schools enforcing unwritten rules?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Albania: Students demand political change and resignation of Prime Minister Edi Rama</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:39408d18bb364063cad853550dde1c9cd4c72bdfa244ecb452951a9b22018067</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T14:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/albania-students-demand-political-change-and-resignation-of-prime-minister-edi-rama/a-79682217--699ae649993b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/albania-students-demand-political-change-and-resignation-of-prime-minister-edi-rama/a-79682217?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Empty lecture halls, burning buildings and demands for change: Albanian students are spearheading a protest movement that has become the biggest challenge to Prime Minister Edi Rama in years.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>The EU wants an AI revolution. But on whose terms?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:95933806ef3eea31981883fdb4d0040d5a29fc6ac3418bc7ecf9e5bcc0b2dc46</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T13:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-eu-wants-an-ai-revolution-but-on-whose-terms/a-79673456--ab198d15d72f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-eu-wants-an-ai-revolution-but-on-whose-terms/a-79673456?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the US and China race ahead, the European Union seeks to boost its economy with AI. Can it compete while protecting workers, safety and the climate?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Italy cuts air traffic in half amid data transmission issue</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8593072d297a85eeab6099c9c09735a64a66b52e55f2e00595e651cca60f7dc6</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T10:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/italy-cuts-air-traffic-in-half-amid-data-transmission-issue/a-79678133--8d0677d89358.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/italy-cuts-air-traffic-in-half-amid-data-transmission-issue/a-79678133?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Citing problems with the data transmission network, Italian authorities have drastically reduced the volume of flights in their airspace. The ENAV authority ruled out malicious activity and said flights remained safe.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Police raid the major pro-opposition Halk TV channel in Turkey</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:83d7b45f0713ae6517ed4fe5f7a0fad78b238370782e0c2fef59c06e1538a449</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T16:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/police-raid-the-major-pro-opposition-halk-tv-channel-in-turkey/a-79671673--402c2b295200.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/police-raid-the-major-pro-opposition-halk-tv-channel-in-turkey/a-79671673?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Turkish police raided the Istanbul headquarters of an important pro-opposition television station on Wednesdazy, the day that jailed Istanbul Mayor Ekrem Imamoglu was set to start his defense against corruption charges.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU summit to focus on China, Ukraine and bloc budget</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2f7aa7649fc7e1f9deee45483124196464705cb088c52ca20d161ad9c6766e91</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T14:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-summit-to-focus-on-china-ukraine-and-bloc-budget/a-79665338--d6856904c849.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-summit-to-focus-on-china-ukraine-and-bloc-budget/a-79665338?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">EU leaders meeting in Brussels will examine measures to curb the bloc's huge trade deficit with China. But they will also be looking to further agreement on the next EU budget ahead of some major elections next year.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Romania: 2 ships on fire in Black Sea, 7 crew missing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:16c4b52d817336bcc47b62e8fd05b7355a4905b3d927bd53cab2207d9c3dc9b9</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T14:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/romania-2-ships-on-fire-in-black-sea-7-crew-missing/a-79667003--b330bc2c57d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/romania-2-ships-on-fire-in-black-sea-7-crew-missing/a-79667003?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two chemical tankers have caught fire in Romanian territorial waters in the Black Sea. The blazes occurred after Russian drones were sighted in Romanian airspace.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Albania: Fire at Education Ministry as students protest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d9aa4ea0531d39dadd766e42477b0f78ac3fc48e6ecd63c89daae99941dd5e1d</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T14:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/albania-fire-at-education-ministry-as-students-protest/a-79661193--fb85f85aef8b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/albania-fire-at-education-ministry-as-students-protest/a-79661193?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Riot police deployed in the Albanian capital Tirana on the second day of student protests. The sudden outbreak seemed at least somewhat reminiscent of the widespread demos in France courting international attention.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: Misleading graph about alleged Russian bot activity</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:51ccd752cc3e1c5b5717d979dfff06273c902ba547d9d241b8b654ccb672d23a</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T09:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-misleading-graph-about-alleged-russian-bot-activity/a-79651769--ec259de6b65a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-misleading-graph-about-alleged-russian-bot-activity/a-79651769?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Did attacks on Russian data centers reduce bot activity around Germany's AfD? A viral graph claims they did. But it contains significant inconsistencies and provides no evidence to support the claim.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine allies in Poland after Starlink sabotage, Trump diesel deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:58683faf5e9caecff6ece8005c13122de5f9a7dfea008301a9754d43a2ef51a5</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T18:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-allies-in-poland-after-starlink-sabotage-trump-diesel-deal/a-79653869--c0d0565fa8d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-allies-in-poland-after-starlink-sabotage-trump-diesel-deal/a-79653869?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's Johann Wadephul said hybrid plots like the Starlink fire showed Europe was "in Russia's crosshairs." The UK's Ed Miliband said Trump's Russian diesel deal led to a "very difficult few days" diplomatically.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine and the US: What's next after Trump's diesel deal with Russia?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2b1dd32a20f376bf5e8b95ec1f30afea3659879549949e0afece3358d32bda11</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T18:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-and-the-us-what-s-next-after-trump-s-diesel-deal-with-russia/a-79650785--59d833db4bc6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-and-the-us-what-s-next-after-trump-s-diesel-deal-with-russia/a-79650785?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump plans to allow the purchase of Russian diesel, drawing criticism at home and abroad. What is behind the US president's decision and what should Ukraine do next? DW spoke with experts.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Critics warn of espionage risks as Slovakia restores military-diplomatic representation with Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e3b595bc2a103616a1fc30431b7d935cf4b600c211cfdc017577ecc1d64bf79</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T12:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/critics-warn-of-espionage-risks-as-slovakia-restores-military-diplomatic-representation-with-russia/a-79649641--99619951a602.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/critics-warn-of-espionage-risks-as-slovakia-restores-military-diplomatic-representation-with-russia/a-79649641?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Slovakia is restoring military-diplomatic relations with Russia for the first time since 2022. The government has defended the move but critics warn of espionage risks and further damage to trust within NATO.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's China calculation shifts as import pressures eclipse export benefits</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1eeb00ef310f4467af20831a689593e94337729c6a3f07cb5d2d50f3bc287484</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T08:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-china-calculation-shifts-as-import-pressures-eclipse-export-benefits/a-79571852--c4df7eb8a062.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-china-calculation-shifts-as-import-pressures-eclipse-export-benefits/a-79571852?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany has long resisted tougher action against China, fearing retaliation. But rising pressure on key industries has pushed Berlin to seek stronger EU trade-defense powers to protect its industrial base.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>What is holding back Cyprus's Schengen ambitions?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7a6f71dbd00f35ddcee7b40053a32828bb42d68b257773f806ab25d11a37e87f</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T06:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-is-holding-back-cyprus-s-schengen-ambitions/a-79641488--5f69812ab764.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-is-holding-back-cyprus-s-schengen-ambitions/a-79641488?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Commission says Cyprus is ready to join the Schengen Area. Yet questions relating to the island's division and British military bases could still complicate its path to Europe's border-free travel zone.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>UK: Iran 'highly likely' to be behind RAF Fairford incident</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7420936ea22a80881858a2f6fb1304768e331abb741a1a319cf56dc900d86fe1</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T19:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-iran-highly-likely-to-be-behind-raf-fairford-incident/a-79645941--7cd1b910595f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-iran-highly-likely-to-be-behind-raf-fairford-incident/a-79645941?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Andy Burnham told parliament there were "strong indications" of Iranian involvement. The government summoned Iran's ambassador. The scare at RAF Fairford led to the withdrawal of USAF B-1 heavy bombers.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Poland reports arrests of 2 Turkish citizens in Germany in connection with Starlink station fire last month</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:220996add2818084a011f4e0a0e855f103ef97f1a2ee1ca8c44d72c92ff44210</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T18:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/poland-reports-arrests-of-2-turkish-citizens-in-germany-in-connection-with-starlink-station-fire-las/a-79646138--0f2bfafb19a7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/poland-reports-arrests-of-2-turkish-citizens-in-germany-in-connection-with-starlink-station-fire-last-month/a-79646138?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Polish authorities have reported the arrests of two Turkish citizens in Germany in connection with alleged sabotage of a Starlink station last month. Prime Minister Donald Tusk called the fire an act of "hybrid warfare."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Who are the Ukrainian 'volunteers' under Russian command?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a172979b8cfe6f4b9514dd045d0f85e1df844b58552d7f55b3337ff84dfec9b8</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T18:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/who-are-the-ukrainian-volunteers-under-russian-command/a-79629555--58ee9f17fd21.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/who-are-the-ukrainian-volunteers-under-russian-command/a-79629555?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia has announced a battalion consisting of Ukrainian "volunteers." But veterans and former prisoners of war share very different accounts.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Trump claims Russia and Ukraine agreed to 'energy ceasefire'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:968991724a55306149dba21afd60bbb3a924d2f842d4c2d7019403bdeaefa892</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T14:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-claims-russia-and-ukraine-agreed-to-energy-ceasefire/a-79634509--966648814544.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-claims-russia-and-ukraine-agreed-to-energy-ceasefire/a-79634509?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump says both sides have agreed to stop targeting oil refineries, power plants and other energy infrastructure immediately.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Georgia's surrogacy industry is booming, but at what cost?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a89ee4a42fbbb5fd4dff60b024b2838a1f5d2a147a99dcae603fc645210eaf34</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T07:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/georgia-s-surrogacy-industry-is-booming-but-at-what-cost/a-79629971--47122bb08522.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/georgia-s-surrogacy-industry-is-booming-but-at-what-cost/a-79629971?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Georgia became a hub for surrogate pregnancies after Russia's full-scale invasion of Ukraine in 2022. DW spoke with parents, and those who wanted to become parents, about the hidden costs of a booming industry.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
